  charges in the future  okay so it's being viewed as a signal  and just to let our viewers know you've  actually been looking at live pictures  there um  phoebe i mean we see the scenes outside  of the courthouse  what is the reaction been there's a lot  going on behind you  yes definitely like just now i'm like  walking out of the club room right after  the judge have finished her sentencing a  lot of supporters inside the courtroom  uh shouted and uh chanted slogans  uh to support the defendants or well  most of them have already been detained  like they want to show support uh before  they were taken away to prison  and maybe to disappear from the public  eye from a certain period of time  and the defendants themselves some of  them  they are responded by chanting slogans  like uh  peaceful rallies is not the crime that  we have spoke to some of the  activists who have come here to attend  the hearing today they  say this is uh literally a chilling  effect that were imposed to the society  because the charges  the conviction and the sentence we're  talking about today is about the  peaceful  protests that it will definitely send a  chilling effect to  other the the peaceful protesters who  want to  organize rallies uh without a permission  from the police  in hong kong thank you  and there are so many concerns about  what these sentences mean for democracy  in hong kong phoebe kang who we just  spoke with there  who uh she had the opportunity to speak  with one defendant the former chairman  of the hong kong democratic party about  how he  sees the increasing crackdown on dissent  a silver medal awarded to young son by  the government for his political work  it was something this former lawmaker  felt proud of  but 12 years later it seems to represent  a hong kong  that's been lost at that time the  central government in beijing  has still uh  adopt a tolerant approach to hong kong  china is my country and hong kong is my  home  but to love your country doesn't 